{{/*
  Targets to delete on apply. chezmoi does not remove a file just because it
  left the source tree — it stops managing it — so a script that is being
  retired needs naming here to actually leave the machines it reached.

  bin/regenerate-completions wrote _just and _chezmoi into brew's
  site-functions. Every completion there is a symlink brew maintains into the
  Cellar, so running it downgraded a self-updating completion to a static file
  frozen at whatever version generated it. Nothing replaces it; there is
  nothing to generate.

  Safe to delete this file once both machines have applied once.
*/ -}}
bin/regenerate-completions

{{/*
  plugins/tmux-navigator.lua declared the Neovim half of vim-tmux-navigator. Its
  four <C-hjkl> mappings moved to config/keymaps.lua as plain wincmd, and the
  plugin went with the tmux half. Deleting the source entry stops chezmoi
  managing the file; it does not remove it, and lazy.nvim keeps loading whatever
  lua/plugins/*.lua it finds — so the plugin stayed installed and its lazy key
  stubs kept shadowing the new mappings until this line existed.
*/ -}}
.config/nvim/lua/plugins/tmux-navigator.lua

{{/*
  .config/bat/themes held a 64KB Catppuccin Mocha .tmTheme. Three separate
  reasons it did nothing: bat only loads a custom theme after `bat cache
  --build` and no cache was ever built, bat 0.26 ships all four Catppuccin
  themes built in, and the config asks for Frappe, not Mocha.
*/ -}}
.config/bat/themes
